## Why This Is Asked

This question tests real-world edge computer vision design with cross-system dataflow: vector search in MongoDB and ERP integration in Oracle, plus hardware constraints and weekly design updates.

## Key Concepts

- Edge inference under strict latency constraints
- 6-DoF pose estimation with known geometry using PnP
- Embedding management and MongoDB Atlas Vector Search
- CDC-style synchronization to Oracle ERP
- On-device 5-10 shot adaptation for evolving pallet designs

## Code Example

```javascript
// PnP pose estimation sketch (OpenCV.js)
function estimatePose(imagePoints, objectPoints, cameraMatrix, distCoeffs) {
  // SolvePnP returns rotation and translation vectors
  const success = cv.solvePnP(
    objectPoints,    // 3D points in object coordinate system
    imagePoints,     // 2D points in image coordinate system
    cameraMatrix,    // Camera intrinsic parameters
    distCoeffs,      // Distortion coefficients
    rvec,            // Output rotation vector
    tvec             // Output translation vector
  );

  if (success) {
    // Convert rotation vector to rotation matrix
    const R = cv.Rodrigues(rvec);
    return { rotation: R, translation: tvec };
  }
  return null;
}
```
